  "explanation": "The av1enc defaults clamp both quantizer bounds to zero. With drop-frame=25 the profile reduces cadence to fit its target; disabling dropping alone restores cadence but exceeds the bitrate target. An explicit 0..63 quantizer range restores cadence while retaining rate control and frame-dropping protection.",
  "reference": "https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/documentation/aom/av1enc.html",
  "scope": [
    "The same immutable static producer binary is used for the three ARM64 diagnostic variants, changing only the stated encoder configuration.",
    "The final reference checks read the committed config.av1.yaml; they do not inject a pipeline override.",
    "These are short direct local tests with a synthetic source; physical cameras, hardware encoders, impaired networks and capture-to-display latency are not qualified here.",
    "The original static functional verdicts remain unchanged; the extra cadence/rate criteria identify why their 8 fps AV1 output was not sufficient performance evidence.",
    "The five camera/test-pattern AV1 YAML files pass configuration validation; only the test-pattern capture source is exercised.",
    "AMD64 runs under Docker Desktop architecture emulation."
  ],
